    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d724">

                <pb facs="0600" n="484" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg484"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/11650.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Letcher to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chihuahua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-22T19:00:00-07:04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 22, 1914, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>General Carranza has privately besought me, as an official who enjoys the respect
                    of the Mexican people and especially those of this party, to approach our
                    President with an earnest plea that some means be found to avoid armed conflict
                    with Mexico while giving due consideration to the sensibilities of the Mexican
                    people.</p>
                <p>They inform me privately that the military leaders to a man united in forcing
                    Carranza to take the stand outlined in his note today relative to the Tampico
                    incident.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Letcher</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
